00:11:28.440 --> 00:11:32.200
So let's click on that.

262
00:11:32.200 --> 00:11:36.559
And we see that we have the new MPC demo there.

263
00:11:36.559 --> 00:11:40.669
And with that set in,

264
00:11:40.669 --> 00:11:43.909
we wanna go ahead and edit some of these.

265
00:11:43.909 --> 00:11:48.669
Now let's actually go to the first key frame

266
00:11:48.669 --> 00:11:50.769
for the rain hit.

267
00:11:50.769 --> 00:11:53.409
And we're gonna hit that plus parameter.

268
00:11:53.409 --> 00:11:55.210
We're gonna load the rough amount.

269
00:11:55.210 --> 00:11:56.929
It's gonna auto key it for us.

270
00:11:56.929 --> 00:11:58.769
Hit that plus parameter again.

271
00:11:59.610 --> 00:12:00.529
And we're gonna load spec amount,

272
00:12:00.529 --> 00:12:02.370
hit that plus parameter again,

273
00:12:02.370 --> 00:12:04.269
and load color in there.

274
00:12:04.269 --> 00:12:07.370
So we're keying all of those for MPC

275
00:12:07.370 --> 00:12:10.679
and we can open it up to see them keyed.

276
00:12:10.679 --> 00:12:12.679
So as I drag it across,

277
00:12:12.679 --> 00:12:14.600
we go all the way over here.

278
00:12:14.600 --> 00:12:18.139
We can now change our color information.

279
00:12:18.139 --> 00:12:20.519
So we can increase the red if we want to,

280
00:12:20.519 --> 00:12:22.240
just a little shiny red.

281
00:12:22.240 --> 00:12:23.919
And you'll see it actually works pretty well

282
00:12:23.919 --> 00:12:25.440
with that blend overlay.

283
00:12:25.440 --> 00:12:28.279
Now again, the blend overlay is gonna react differently

284
00:12:28.320 --> 00:12:29.159
like in Photoshop,

285
00:12:29.159 --> 00:12:31.639
depending on what your material and texture is like,

286
00:12:31.639 --> 00:12:32.879
but that just showed you one way

287
00:12:32.879 --> 00:12:34.679
to be able to blend them.

288
00:12:34.679 --> 00:12:37.220
We can now go in here under spec amount

289
00:12:37.220 --> 00:12:40.059
and we can increase or decrease things

290
00:12:40.059 --> 00:12:42.139
according to what we need.

291
00:12:42.139 --> 00:12:43.299
Now, if you want to,

292
00:12:43.299 --> 00:12:44.799
we have it set default to one,

293
00:12:44.799 --> 00:12:46.860
we can set that to zero

294
00:12:46.860 --> 00:12:49.659
and we can do spec to one.

295
00:12:49.659 --> 00:12:52.039
And you'll see we actually have it nice and shiny

296
00:12:52.039 --> 00:12:54.019
and they're complimenting each other.

297
00:12:54.019 --> 00:12:56.580
Notice that spec was turning everything off.

298
00:12:56.580 --> 00:13:00.139
So we can now have that all key framed in here

299
00:13:00.139 --> 00:13:03.820
and we can now see this sphere start to change color

300
00:13:03.820 --> 00:13:06.460
and get wet in our scene.

301
00:13:06.460 --> 00:13:07.870
Pretty cool.

302
00:13:07.870 --> 00:13:08.850
All right.

303
00:13:08.850 --> 00:13:10.610
Well, that's about it with this one.

304
00:13:10.610 --> 00:13:12.049
Hope this makes sense to you

305
00:13:12.049 --> 00:13:15.490
and helps you kind of navigate using MPCs.

306
00:13:15.490 --> 00:13:16.809
Materials are very tricky

307
00:13:16.809 --> 00:13:18.730
and the fact that you want to make sure their state

308
00:13:18.730 --> 00:13:21.970
is in a neutral state or a nice starting point

309
00:13:21.970 --> 00:13:23.370
to bring them into sequencer

310
00:13:23.370 --> 00:13:25.330
and to get them to read accordingly.

311
00:13:25.330 --> 00:13:26.970
Notice we're not controlling the range.

312
00:13:26.970 --> 00:13:29.330
So you do need to know your numbers ahead of time.

313
00:13:29.330 --> 00:13:30.809
So just keep those things in mind.

314
00:13:30.809 --> 00:13:32.110
That's it with this video.

315
00:13:32.110 --> 00:13:32.950
In the next video,

